Identity Resolution
Deduplicates and unifies customer records by resolving identities across channels and devices to a single individual or household.
Plain terms: You have "Rob Smith," "Robert Smith" and "R. Smith" in three systems. This tells you they're one person.
Example: A bank's CRM has 12M records but only 8M real people. You've been emailing the same person 3 times and counting them 3 times in reporting. 
